From c382c4fd870a894835511c6a5fd64fbc29c79a40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 05:56:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 131/133] dynarmic A64: forward CBZ/CBNZ/TBZ/TBNZ as side
 exits; float stores straight from XMM registers

superblocks: a forward CBZ, CBNZ, TBZ or TBNZ (IL2CPP's null checks, flag tests: each a block of
two or three instructions before) doesn't end the block: A64ExitIfZero32/64 and A64ExitIfTestBit
(test r, r or test/bt; a jcc to a link of its own in the cold code), the code after it translated
on into the block (eight a block at most, its first 64 instructions); A64GetSetElimination keeps
what was set before each exit, the dead flags pass stops at it. A 32- or 64-bit plain store whose
value is in an XMM (STR S/D, a float result) is a movd/movq from it (new fallback stubs) instead of
a move to a general register first. unity.c (IL2CPP-shaped): 22% fewer block entries, -3.0%
instructions; game.c -0.4%.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
